  {
    "id": "N029V/components",
    "family": "components",
    "prompt": "Write Python function solve. Given n>=0 and list edges of undirected edges [u,v], vertices are 0..n-1. Return the number of connected components, counting isolated vertices. Self-edges and repeated edges are allowed. Return only the complete function after any thinking. Do not import modules.",
    "solution": "def solve(n,edges):\n    graph=[[] for j in range(n)]\n    for a,b in edges:\n        graph[a].append(b)\n        graph[b].append(a)\n    seen=set()\n    count=0\n    for v in range(n):\n        if v in seen: continue\n        count+=1\n        stack=[v]\n        seen.add(v)\n        while stack:\n            x=stack.pop()\n            for y in graph[x]:\n                if y not in seen:\n                    seen.add(y)\n                    stack.append(y)\n    return count",
    "cases": [
